{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata","id":1245691,"title":"Polishing Gold - what Solar Charms would you like to receive errata?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-13T17:56:51-07:00","id":1245691,"title":"Polishing Gold - what Solar Charms would you like to receive errata?","content":"In some cases, one might think a perfectly functional Charm is written in a misleading fashion and could use clarification; like how Monkey Leap Technique seems to supplement a Move or Disengage action (and therefore working within existing rules) rather than substituting for your movement action and venturing into uncharted territory in regards to what is permitted.<br /> <br /> In other cases, you might think that a Charm is a left-over relic from a previous iteration; like how Demon-Wasting Rush is in many respects an inferior version of Godspeed Steps (which doesn't count it as a prerequisite) with one particular advantage, but no synergy for knowing both Charms.<br /> <br /> And then there's people's complaints about the Crafting Project slots of the Craft trees.<br /> <br /> For my own part, I wonder if Hammer Thunder Hammer shouldn't have split off the option to punch enemies straight up into the sky (or ceilings, for double falling damage) as a upgrade Charm that reused the name &quot;Dome-Shattering Smite&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> The original developers and writers did a fantastic job, and Third Edition doesn't need any errata nearly on the level of First Edition's &quot;power combat&quot; or Second Edition's &quot;Dawn Solution&quot;, but nothing is perfect and the first book always has to learn the Edition's lessons too quickly.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, yeah, and someone leaked the playtesting document and got the tests shut down prematurely. That probably didn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> So, what are the Charms that you think need another evaluation, and what do you think should be done to them?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT 2:<br /> <br /> <b>Can we all just agree that this thread isn't about examining whether or not Charms are appropriately &quot;Solar&quot; or &quot;belonging to this or that Ability&quot; and that it is solely about pointing out areas where the mechanics are unclear, too weak, or too strong?<br /> <br /> &quot;Solar Lore shouldn't do that!&quot; is an entirely separate discussion worthy of its own thread.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-11-2019, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T18:16:41-07:00","id":1245701,"title":"","content":"The charms that are clearly not solar, like the lore prophesy charm, and celestial bliss trick (which was a sidereal ability before). And a bunch of charms that are unclear and had to be verified how they work because the wording was unclear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T21:05:34-07:00","id":1245743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245701#post1245701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The charms that are clearly not solar, like the lore prophesy charm, and celestial bliss trick (which was a sidereal ability before).</div> </div> </div> </div>It might still be one again in a modified form, you know. In any case, if sex is practice in which someone can excel... Solars get to go there. There wasn't any thematic protection that it necessarily had, much as how Solars can train people to be better soldiers or sailors, and there is also a power that Sidereals got in The Captain that allowed them to train and organize soldiers and sailors, because the constellation is all about hard-assed discipline and overlaps with certain aspects of Solar Sail and War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-14-2018, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T21:42:43-07:00","id":1245749,"title":"","content":"I know that at one point the plan was definitely for both Solars and Sidereals to have Celestial Bliss Trick. Obviously that might have changed.<br /> <br /> (Personally I feel that while Solars can definitely do &quot;put someone under your sway via sex&quot;, I always felt that the somewhat clinical and transactional nature of Celestial Bliss Trick was meant to be a commentary on Venus' views on sex. The difference is a bit subtle - Solar sex charms, like most of Solar performance, should be, thematically, more &quot;I'm so awesomely sexy that it's natural for you to want to serve me!&quot;, much like X-Seducing-Demon-Dance. Whereas Celestial Bliss Trick feels like it cuts away the romance and goes straight to overtly stating &quot;sex is a way to control people.&quot;)<br /> <br /> But to take a step back, that's probably just because I know it was originally a Sidereal power. If it had been in the Solar charmset first, I doubt anyone would have said &quot;oh, this looks like it should be a Sidereal thing!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-14-2018, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T21:47:55-07:00","id":1245751,"title":"","content":"Wyld Shaping technique needs a complete overhaul. I've encountered about half a dozen different ways that people have interpreted that single charm leading to thousands of square miles of differentiation in result. Plus wyld called weapon probably shouldn't be able to pull an Artifact N/A weapon out of the wyld period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T22:47:43-07:00","id":1245768,"title":"","content":"Racing Hare Method and Mountain-Crossing Leap need proper long distance speeds given.<br /> <br /> That Brawl charm for Feats of Strength needs to be rewritten to work with the Feats of Strength system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T00:00:02-07:00","id":1245785,"title":"","content":"Elusive Dream Defense is very underwhelming and at times can be a disadvantage since defensive intimacies can grant more bonus then offensive ones. I feel it should also add 1 non charm defense to both guile and resolve for the rest of the scene and maybe an essence 5 upgrade that denys essence successes gained through either non charm dice added through magic or successes added through non 10 doubles or successes gained from numbers less than 7 from magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T00:10:13-07:00","id":1245786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245785#post1245785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elusive Dream Defense is very underwhelming and at times can be a disadvantage since defensive intimacies can grant more bonus then offensive ones. I feel it should also add 1 non charm defense to both guile and resolve for the rest of the scene and maybe an essence 5 upgrade that denys essence successes gained through either non charm dice added through magic or successes added through non 10 doubles or successes gained from numbers less than 7 from magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That second option way too strong. You might as well block all magic at that point. Cancelling out automatic successes or dice from a charm wouldn't be too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T02:26:09-07:00","id":1245804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245786#post1245786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That second option way too strong. You might as well block all magic at that point. Cancelling out automatic successes or dice from a charm wouldn't be too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that but at that essence level for a once per story charm i feel it might be needed to overcome some High essence gods charms on the scale of the elemental dragons Censors geas charm. Solars need these super charms or how can they face things like the Ebon dragon in conversation. But your point is good. How about a charm that enhances it like you suggested instead but can then reset the charm or enhance it even more when faced with a truely dangerous foe.<br /> <br /> new elusive dream defense same cost also grants 1 auto noncharm defense to your social defense.<br /> <br /> new charm. Name needed. enhances elusive dream defense allowing the solar to subtract up to essence successes for every 1 in her opponent's roll up to essence times during the scene. vs a foe who is at essence 6 + allow the solar to instead pay 10m 1wp to have the guile or resolve be added as non charm.vs them for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T02:42:41-07:00","id":1245810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245768#post1245768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Racing Hare Method and Mountain-Crossing Leap need proper long distance speeds given.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that. I noted it during the playtest but I didn't make a big issue over it because at the time I assumed we were eventually going to get an explaination of out of combat speeds measured range bands when we got to travel sorcery like Stormwind Rider. Instead the playtest got ended early and as you saw Stormwind Rider's speed ended up being conveyed in miles per hour.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T03:40:29-07:00","id":1245817,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm misunderstanding them, but Bottomless Wellspring Approach and Lore-Inducing Concentration seem pretty underpowered to me. I wonder if they're meant to be speed-bumps on the way to Wyld-Shaping Technique? On WST itself, I don't know that I'd go so far as to say that it needs a complete overhaul, but some clarification on the details would be welcome.<br /> <br /> Clarification on Awakening Eye supplementing &quot;a Join Battle roll with a free full (Perception + Awareness) Excellency&quot; would be nice. I saw a few people asking about it in the Ask the Devs thread, and maybe it got a more definite answer than the first that I saw, but that thread's currently at 889 pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T04:03:53-07:00","id":1245822,"title":"","content":"I think Prophet-Uplifting Evocation could use some fleshing out. Like, how does their essence pool work? &quot;four motes, plus up to five more&quot;. Does that mean they get an essence pool of between four and nine motes depending on what the solar felt like giving them, or is it a regular pool of four motes plus a five mote pool that the solar has to refill themselves? <br /> <br /> And what can they do with it? 3e doesn't really like giving people an essence pool for it's own sake. These guys are supposed to be prophets of a solar. They need more than just one integrity charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T04:06:34-07:00","id":1245823,"title":"","content":"The full free excellency was pretty definitely addressed in relation to another thread a bit ago. You get +X charm dice for 0m/etc.applied to the roll with all the normal restrictions on Excellency Charm dice. If your Perception is higher than your Wits, you don't roll more dice than you'd be able to with just boosting JB with the Awareness Excellency, because the base dice-pool still caps. Likewise if you have lower Perception than Wits, since Perception is specified (not all Charms force a specific roll on you), you can't add more dice than Perception + Awareness despite not hitting the cap. And like any other Excellency, if you have other sources of Charm dice/successes already, they apply to the cap of how much you can add.<br /> <br /> Was there still some lingering confusion about how those are supposed to work?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T05:51:00-07:00","id":1245842,"title":"","content":"I never had any problem with &quot;roll X <b>with</b> a free full excellency&quot;. That seems obvious: you get to use your excellency for free, with as many dice as you can get like normal.<br /> <br /> I did wonder about some of the charms that say &quot;roll a full Int+Craft excellency&quot; or something like that. Because it seems like you roll the excellency, but not the normal dice?<br /> That's more a clarification than an errata though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry about that. I noted it during the playtest but I didn't make a big issue over it because at the time I assumed we were eventually going to get an explaination of out of combat speeds measured range bands when we got to travel sorcery like Stormwind Rider. Instead the playtest got ended early and as you saw Stormwind Rider's speed ended up being conveyed in miles per hour. </div> </div> </div>Unless you were the one who leaked things, I can't really blame you for that. It is the kind of thing where you assume there'll be an explanation somewhere, especially as there's more than one charm that talk about moving multiple range bands outside combat, and you'd assume there'll be some &quot;Range bands generally equal about X feet&quot; like most games do.<br /> <br /> I assume with Stormwind Rider and the flying cloud (I can't remember what it's called right now), they're written a different way because a different person wrote them.<br /> Though the Ride long-distance charm is also written a different way (to both). Though maybe it has to, to take into account the different speed of different animals (I remember the 2nd ed charm where riding an elephant was way faster over long distances than riding a horse).<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't remember it, but someone might know the name: There's a Dodge charm where when they ambush you, your Evasion is like 2+the number of 1s they roll, something like that. And if you reach your full Evasion, you can boost it further with Dodge charms. Which means people with a lower Evasion are better against ambushes than people with high Evasion, which is kind of stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-14-2018, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:50:55-07:00","id":1245898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245804#post1245804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that but at that essence level for a once per story charm i feel it might be needed to overcome some High essence gods charms on the scale of the elemental dragons Censors geas charm. Solars need these super charms or how can they face things like the Ebon dragon in conversation. But your point is good. How about a charm that enhances it like you suggested instead but can then reset the charm or enhance it even more when faced with a truely dangerous foe.<br /> <br /> new elusive dream defense same cost also grants 1 auto noncharm defense to your social defense.<br /> <br /> new charm. Name needed. enhances elusive dream defense allowing the solar to subtract up to essence successes for every 1 in her opponent's roll up to essence times during the scene. vs a foe who is at essence 6 + allow the solar to instead pay 10m 1wp to have the guile or resolve be added as non charm.vs them for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't let there be any scene long defense increase in the game. Solars don't have one in with physical attacks. They shouldn't have a socialize one. Especially not with the the mote generation from combat. It should be motes per attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:52:57-07:00","id":1245900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245842#post1245842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't remember it, but someone might know the name: There's a Dodge charm where when they ambush you, your Evasion is like 2+the number of 1s they roll, something like that. And if you reach your full Evasion, you can boost it further with Dodge charms. Which means people with a lower Evasion are better against ambushes than people with high Evasion, which is kind of stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surprise anticipation technique and it does need a buff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:31:10-07:00","id":1245915,"title":"","content":"This might be too broad for the topic, but Lore is just a weird grab bag of ideas. Learning, Teaching, Knowing, Extrapolating, Exploiting, Inferring, all good.<br /> <br /> However, Wyld dispelling Prana, Essence Lending, Wound Accepting Technique? These aren't lore based at all. It feels like half the team heard &quot;Make charms for Essence Manipulation&quot; and half the team heard &quot;Make charms about being a Master Scholar&quot;.<br /> <br /> Injury Forcing Technique? What the actual hell even is this. It could fit Medicine, Brawl, or Occult <i>maybe</i>. if you did a blind charm preview and asked us to guess what tree it goes in, I would never have picked Lore. A Larceny capstone? that would be legendary. Lore?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:36:35-07:00","id":1245920,"title":"","content":"Lore includes science, and for Exalted, science teaches them how to do more things with their Essence.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why Dragon-Blooded can use it to give each other Aura and throw elemental blasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:43:59-07:00","id":1245923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245898#post1245898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't let there be any scene long defense increase in the game. Solars don't have one in with physical attacks. They shouldn't have a socialize one. Especially not with the the mote generation from combat. It should be motes per attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see much relation between socialise charms and mote generation in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:45:54-07:00","id":1245924,"title":"","content":"Ok, I get the logic of injury-forcing technique. Lore charms have this thing where they let you muck about with stuff on the character sheet. It's a bit fourth wall breaky, but essence, willpower and health all fall under the wheelhouse of resources that get used to fuel charms. They're connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:05:34-07:00","id":1245938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245898#post1245898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't let there be any scene long defense increase in the game. Solars don't have one in with physical attacks. They shouldn't have a socialize one. Especially not with the the mote generation from combat. It should be motes per attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elusive dream defense is a scene long defense enhancing charm. Social combat doesnt regen motes like normal combat so scene long defenses should be alright especially at the once per story level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:46:13-07:00","id":1245960,"title":"","content":"Divine Mantle jumps out at me. Not sure what you would rewrite it to, but it certainly could use... something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:03:18-07:00","id":1245970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245923#post1245923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see much relation between socialise charms and mote generation in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have misread it then. I always thought it was across the board but even without it. I wouldn't give it that much power. I'd still add a cost to activate it if it's going to just negate a massive bonus like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:25:39-07:00","id":1245984,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, definitely<br /> <br /> Oh, I've just thought of Words-As-Workshop. It's a fine concept, but... it basically doesn't have any rules. You might a bonus. A mechanical bonus. Of... who knows how much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:26:23-07:00","id":1246164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245823#post1245823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The full free excellency was pretty definitely addressed in relation to another thread a bit ago. You get +X charm dice for 0m/etc.applied to the roll with all the normal restrictions on Excellency Charm dice. If your Perception is higher than your Wits, you don't roll more dice than you'd be able to with just boosting JB with the Awareness Excellency, because the base dice-pool still caps. Likewise if you have lower Perception than Wits, since Perception is specified (not all Charms force a specific roll on you), you can't add more dice than Perception + Awareness despite not hitting the cap. And like any other Excellency, if you have other sources of Charm dice/successes already, they apply to the cap of how much you can add.<br /> <br /> Was there still some lingering confusion about how those are supposed to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm guessing that's from deeper in the thread than I reached before giving up. It sounds workable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T21:58:09-07:00","id":1246181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245920#post1245920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore includes science, and for Exalted, science teaches them how to do more things with their Essence.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why Dragon-Blooded can use it to give each other Aura and throw elemental blasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Health Stealing makes sense in Lore because Lore is Science and Science is Soul Power and stealing health is a Soul Thing&quot;. Sure, when you define it tautologically like that it makes sense, but so does anything. &quot;Blood Spilling is an act of Combat and combat is Melee so there's a Melee charm to Steal Blood and heal yourself&quot;. &quot;Life is a thing you possess and taking possessions is Larceny so Life Steal is Larceny&quot;. Blood Letting is Medicine. Essence Manipulation is Occult. ABC is XYZ.<br /> <br /> Honest to god here, if I showed you a charm preview of Wound Accepting Technique and Injury Forcing Technique with no flavor text, would you seriously have guessed <b>Lore</b>?<br /> <br /> Edit: Just in case you meant about Wyld Shaping and the others- that doesn't cry out Occult to you? because using essence to manipulate the unnatural world of the Wyld does not say to me &quot;A reasonably well read man could do this&quot;. It says to me &quot;A person who works with magic and spirits could do this&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 08-15-2018, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:46:21-07:00","id":1246196,"title":"","content":"I thought that, but someone on this forum pointed out to me that in order to create animals, plants, land, metal, etc, you have to understand their properties, and that's Lore.<br /> <br /> I agree with you about Injury-Forcing Discipline though. (It used to be an Abyssal Lore charm actually, IIRC)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T23:11:21-07:00","id":1246200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246196#post1246196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that, but someone on this forum pointed out to me that in order to create animals, plants, land, metal, etc, you have to understand their properties, and that's Lore.<br /> <br /> I agree with you about Injury-Forcing Discipline though. (It used to be an Abyssal Lore charm actually, IIRC)</div> </div> </div> </div>Injury-Forcing Technique originally appeared in CB: Twilight, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T04:58:34-07:00","id":1246260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245842#post1245842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember it, but someone might know the name: There's a Dodge charm where when they ambush you, your Evasion is like 2+the number of 1s they roll, something like that. And if you reach your full Evasion, you can boost it further with Dodge charms. Which means people with a lower Evasion are better against ambushes than people with high Evasion, which is kind of stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there are not many dodge charms that are valid to use even once you reach your full evasion, because the attack roll has already occurred. At a brief glance the best you could do is make them miss on rolling equal to your evasion with drifting leaf elusion. Which is yet more reason why I would like that charm reviewed as the current wording is a bit of a trap.<br /> <br /> For my charm choices I would have to go with Nine Aeons Thew &amp; Ten Ox Meditation. Nine Aeons Thew with its double 7s and ignoring strength requirement really does make any feat of strength possible even with strength 1 when combined with charms in its Prerequisite chain. Essentially it makes feats of strength too easy for a supernal athletics character that you don't even need to invest in strength. I would dare say that if you want to make a character that feats of strength is their thing you should go straight for Nine Aeons Thew and at most strength 3. Any more strength would be a waste, and to achieve the top feats of strength you will want Nine Aeons Thew anyway.<br /> <br /> With Ten Ox Meditation its effect is just underwhelming. It sits in a gap of if athletics is not supernal then sure get it, but only after essence 2 when you can pick up Thunder's Might to give you enough potential successes to be able to use it. Before that it will just let a strength 3 or 4 character possibly push strength 5 feats. Then you compare its effect to the artifact Dauntless - where you can commit an extra 4 motes to get 1 automatic non-charm success and have your strength count as 3 higher to determine what feats you can do when lifting or breaking an object.<br /> <br /> One last one would be Armored Scout's Invigoration. Overall it looks nice, and if Arms of the Chosen hadn't been released I wouldn't be mentioning it. In this case Mela's Coil being heavy armor and providing no mobility penalty for no extra charge is why the call out here. If the effect of removing a mobility penalty can be tacked onto an artifact essentially as a free evocation with no mote cost then I can't see how a solar charm that you have to pay xp for and pay a mote cost for to activate to get the same effect can be justified.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T05:06:27-07:00","id":1246263,"title":"","content":"Hmm, do you think Ten Ox meditation would be more functional with a better success to strength dot conversion? <br /> <br /> It's still rendered obsolete by Nine Aeons Thew, of course, barring situations where one is out of willpower, but 9AT <i>is</i> a capstone. Perhaps we could throw in a clause that makes Ten Ox do something else when used in conjunction or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T06:58:14-07:00","id":1246310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1245810#post1245810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry about that. I noted it during the playtest but I didn't make a big issue over it because at the time I assumed we were eventually going to get an explaination of out of combat speeds measured range bands when we got to travel sorcery like Stormwind Rider. Instead the playtest got ended early and as you saw Stormwind Rider's speed ended up being conveyed in miles per hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope that in this edition they choose to give Racing Hare a better overland speed than 'worse than Storwind Rider in every conceivable way'. I fee that in 3rd, it'd be even more egrarious, since you don't spend motes on spells anymore, and you even get the willpower back! Solar speed charms need some love! <br /> <br /> Socialize Persona Charms: On what else I'd like to see needing an errata, the Socialize Persona Charms would need some errata on the requirements. Do the persona needs to have socialize 5 to return to the old self? Which of the new charms of the persona supersede the central character's charms, and which remain? <br /> <br /> Combat Groups x Charms: Also, I would ike to see the integration between several of the combat charms and the combat groups rules. Why is Dipping Swallow Defense and other Onslaught negating charms useless against a combat group, when it is a charm made to defend against multiple oponents? Some effect should be here. How do Charms that work against decisive damage only work against a Combat Group? What are the benefits of area attack charms, such as Dancing Devil Trigger Finger, against Combat Groups?<br /> <br /> Integrity - Inviolable Essence-Merging: In what timing can it be used? If it can be used in the normal timing, then it's a 2nd ed Perfect Defense right here, down to a limitation. I don't think the intent of the charm is for it to be played as a tactical combat charm, otherwise it's a terrible precedent for this edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T07:16:04-07:00","id":1246320,"title":"","content":"I don't think Nine Aeons Thew making high strength superfluous for Feats of Strength is a problem - I mean, if you buy that many Resistance charms, and you're Resistance Supernal, having Stamina greater than 3 is overkill for resisting diseases,<br /> <br /> It is a bit odd that it makes several earlier Charms obsolete, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:03:20-07:00","id":1246365,"title":"","content":"Found it! Old thread about Ten Ox Meditation (well eventually):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1073597-ex3-increasing-strength-excercise\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1073597-ex3-increasing-strength-excercise\"> [Ex3] Increasing Strength Excercise - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1073597-ex3-increasing-strength-excercise\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1073597-ex3-increasing-strength-excercise </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So what does the forum think of an athletics charm that allows you to commit motes to ISE to keep it active indefinitely? I like to play the strongman, and I would like the peace of mind to activate it and just keep it on, instead of having to say I reactivate it every scene. Also, anyone have any cool ideas for any additional Athletics charms, or strongman builds, that emphasize overwhelming might, in and/or out of combat? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T15:05:54-07:00","id":1246441,"title":"","content":"As far as Lore charms go, I think the ones that mess with xp deserve looking at, since xp is a PC only construct. Just handing out an xp bonus doesn\u2019t really make sense for teaching NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T15:06:45-07:00","id":1246442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246260#post1246260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Ten Ox Meditation its effect is just underwhelming. It sits in a gap of if athletics is not supernal then sure get it, but only after essence 2 when you can pick up Thunder's Might to give you enough potential successes to be able to use it. Before that it will just let a strength 3 or 4 character possibly push strength 5 feats. Then you compare its effect to the artifact Dauntless - where you can commit an extra 4 motes to get 1 automatic non-charm success and have your strength count as 3 higher to determine what feats you can do when lifting or breaking an object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it sounded pretty impressive until I did the math and found out my Night with Str 4, Athletics 4 could... spend a full Excellency to get even odds of pulling a wagon or bending a horseshoe. Those upper Strength 5+ feats are pretty statistically unlikely without other Charms enhancing the attempt, and Strength 7+ are just out of the question. If I need to smash through any brick walls or fortress gates, I'd better hope there's someone else around I can Heaven Thunder Hammer through them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T17:29:25-07:00","id":1246481,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not totally sure how you\u2019d fix this while keeping its spirit intact, but Open Palm Caress is the only charm in the game that explicitly wants you to be <i>bad</i> at something, which is a really awkward design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T19:35:07-07:00","id":1246516,"title":"","content":"Can we all just agree that this thread isn't about examining whether or not Charms are appropriately &quot;Solar&quot; or &quot;belonging to this or that Ability&quot; and that it is solely about pointing out areas where the mechanics are unclear, too weak, or too strong?<br /> <br /> &quot;Solar Lore shouldn't do that!&quot; is an entirely separate discussion worthy of its own thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T20:28:44-07:00","id":1246526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246481#post1246481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not totally sure how you\u2019d fix this while keeping its spirit intact, but Open Palm Caress is the only charm in the game that explicitly wants you to be <i>bad</i> at something, which is a really awkward design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would make more sense if it rewarded you for rolling better than anyone else, but delaying your turn until at least the action of your fastest opponent. It might enhance your Join Battle roll, with the limitations that you can't be wearing any armor or holding a weapon, and you must delay if you beat all opponents.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it could let you reflexively roll (Manipulation + Presence) at the start of the fight to see how many people you fool, and let you drain Initiative from the fooled parties as written.<br /> <br /> Something like that.<br /> <br /> I always saw the name to mean that you started a fight with a slap, which everyone else was supposed to mistake for something other than an attack. The name doesn't make as much sense if you can't use the Charm to start the fight with the first attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T21:41:09-07:00","id":1246535,"title":"","content":"Splendid magpie approach should most likely be rolled into Cunning mimicry technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T01:05:07-07:00","id":1246566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246441#post1246441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Lore charms go, I think the ones that mess with xp deserve looking at, since xp is a PC only construct. Just handing out an xp bonus doesn\u2019t really make sense for teaching NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stern Tutor Discipline from the Dragon-Blooded book is so much cleaner in this regard. I doubt it would be that hard to houserule, but if this hypothetical errata did happen, I would like to see Flowing Mind Prana done like the Dragon-Blooded variant.<br /> <br /> For those who don't have the Kickstarter text: Stern Tutor Discipline is similar to Flowing Mind Prana except the DB doesn't have to spend XP, they just allow the other character to go into debt, and if it's used on NPC's it doesn't use the normal XP system at all, it just gives them a specialty or dot after a certain time spent training.<br /> <hr /><br /> There is one additional problem I have with a few of the Solar charms: Divine Mantle and Carnal Spirit Rending.<br /> They put in an <b>Eclipse</b> keyword to mark spirit/fae charms that are safe for PC's to have access to. And then you add solar charms that ignore that keyword.<br /> I believe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1193684#post1193684\">Vance has mentioned that he doesn't think the Solars should be able to break this rule.</a><br /> And to clarify: I'm not worried about power level concerns with these charms, I just think they set a bad precedent and might put ST's in a bad spot where they now have to go against the letter of the charm to preserve the integrity of their game (which they should be able to, but it's never a nice feeling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8097,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","user":"wern212","date":".  Added my issues with Divine Mantle and Carnal Spirit Rending. 08-16-2018, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:11:56-07:00","id":1246683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246566#post1246566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stern Tutor Discipline from the Dragon-Blooded book is so much cleaner in this regard. I doubt it would be that hard to houserule, but if this hypothetical errata did happen, I would like to see Flowing Mind Prana done like the Dragon-Blooded variant.<br /> <br /> For those who don't have the Kickstarter text: Stern Tutor Discipline is similar to Flowing Mind Prana except the DB doesn't have to spend XP, they just allow the other character to go into debt, and if it's used on NPC's it doesn't use the normal XP system at all, it just gives them a specialty or dot after a certain time spent training.<br /> <hr /><br /> There is one additional problem I have with a few of the Solar charms: Divine Mantle and Carnal Spirit Rending.<br /> They put in an <b>Eclipse</b> keyword to mark spirit/fae charms that are safe for PC's to have access to. And then you add solar charms that ignore that keyword.<br /> I believe <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1193684#post1193684\">Vance has mentioned that he doesn't think the Solars should be able to break this rule.</a><br /> And to clarify: I'm not worried about power level concerns with these charms, I just think they set a bad precedent and might put ST's in a bad spot where they now have to go against the letter of the charm to preserve the integrity of their game (which they should be able to, but it's never a nice feeling).</div> </div> </div> </div>Divine Mantle's &quot;miracle&quot; terminology is also a tad annoying to me--I think it's meant to imply things that aren't charms but are in a spirit's purview? I don't mind the concept of &quot;Get thematic powers by having spirits recognize your right to rule&quot; but they feel...to vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T07:24:16-07:00","id":1249961,"title":"","content":"I really feel like Blood and Salt Bondage needs a cap of some sort. It's pretty good on a normal ship, but the second you include an artifact ship, doesn't even need to be Horizon Endeavor, it ramps up way too quickly. Personally, I think capping each type of HL to the user's essence would work. (I.E Character has ess. 3, the max he can get/give would be 3x-0, 3x-1, 3x-2 and 3xincap)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23809-orukan","name":"Orukan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T19:16:42-07:00","id":1252907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Red-Toothed Execution Order,&quot; Exalted pp. 413</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it is a reflexive, this Charm supplements<br /> a familiar\u2019s <b>decisive</b> attack, adding extra successes<br /> to the attack\u2019s raw damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in this charm's description does it say how <i>many</i> extra successes are added to the raw damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T19:32:39-07:00","id":1252911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1252907#post1252907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere in this charm's description does it say how <i>many</i> extra successes are added to the raw damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does, actually: &quot;adding extra successes from the attack roll to the attack\u2019s raw damage.&quot; Normal decisive attacks don't add any extra successes from the attack roll to the damage roll, so this charm is basically just changing that - any extra successes you get on the attack roll, are added to the damage roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T19:43:34-07:00","id":1252913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246516#post1246516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we all just agree that this thread isn't about examining whether or not Charms are appropriately &amp;quot;Solar&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;belonging to this or that Ability&amp;quot; and that it is solely about pointing out areas where the mechanics are unclear, too weak, or too strong?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Solar Lore shouldn't do that!&amp;quot; is an entirely separate discussion worthy of its own thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem there is errata has specifically included that kind of thing before, so it... sort of is, although I agree it is worth a full thread.<br /> <br /> Although, briefly: if one accepts the 3e version of Lore as acting akin to the metaplay of other games, allowing one to establish facts that do not contradict existing facts, then Solar Lore makes perfect sense as a powered up version of this, with the same limits. A Solar may predict a doom will befall their foe, as befits those who act against the Chosen of the Most High. Sidereal fate-meddling, however, is *not* metaplay, and they are free to make it so that city has always been ten miles east of where the flood will hit, as of a week ago. In a battle between facts and a Sidereal, the Sidereal wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T00:06:53-07:00","id":1252975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1252911#post1252911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It does, actually: &quot;adding extra successes from the attack roll to the attack\u2019s raw damage.&quot; Normal decisive attacks don't add any extra successes from the attack roll to the damage roll, so this charm is basically just changing that - any extra successes you get on the attack roll, are added to the damage roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. That makes sense. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T05:38:33-07:00","id":1253028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1246310#post1246310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Socialize Persona Charms: On what else I'd like to see needing an errata, the Socialize Persona Charms would need some errata on the requirements. Do the persona needs to have socialize 5 to return to the old self? Which of the new charms of the persona supersede the central character's charms, and which remain? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A persona with the later charms has entirely new stats and charms. However, they know who they are. The problem with this is that the character is comparable to a low stated mortal with charms. It takes hundreds of xp for them to be viable. Take it from personal experience, stop at the charm at that gives your persona motivations and intimacies or work with your st to completely rework how those later charms work. I don't think vance and eric have the time to fix them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 09-10-2018, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:41:34-07:00","id":1253123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1253028#post1253028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A persona with the later charms has entirely new stats and charms. However, they know who they are. The problem with this is that the character is comparable to a low stated mortal with charms. It takes hundreds of xp for them to be viable. Take it from personal experience, stop at the charm at that gives your persona motivations and intimacies or work with your st to completely rework how those later charms work. I don't think vance and eric have the time to fix them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't work with the GM. *I'm* the pagliacci!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:47:19-07:00","id":1253124,"title":"","content":"Well, in that case just make two characters and quietly swap sheets when nobody is looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T13:54:19-07:00","id":1253127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1245691-polishing-gold-what-solar-charms-would-you-like-to-receive-errata?p=1253123#post1253123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can't work with the GM. *I'm* the pagliacci!</div> </div> </div> </div>If a player wants to use them the only way to make them viable is to just let them shift dots around and take a hit by only being able to take half of their new charms<br /> <br /> The biggest problems with persona are just how poorly stated they are and exp. Losing access to half your charms sucks but it's not as bad as only having like fraction of your abilities. The second issue is managing the xp which is really just dumb. I would just limit it to half their current charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 09-10-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}